cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use KSA Rail Twin, please cite it with the metadata below. Every modelled
  output is synthetic demand, uncalibrated: scenario comparison, not a forecast.
  It is an independent simulation, not a government plan. Version 1.0.0 is
  the first public release (code published; native Saudi review of the
  Arabic pending; films follow the review).
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/alturkestani/KSA-RailTwin"
url: "https://github.com/alturkestani/KSA-RailTwin"
title: KSA Rail Twin
authors:
  - family-names: Alturkestani
    given-names: Tariq
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  KSA Rail Twin is a personal, open-source and non-partisan economic feasibility
  study of a national rail network for Saudi Arabia: which corridors, in what
  order, at what cost, with what long-term benefit, funded and delivered how,
  and with what effect on people, benchmarked against other countries'
  experience. Simulation is the tool; the decision case is the product. It
  covers a Kingdom-wide screening of all 13 regions, cost estimates with
  reference-class uplifts, demand and mode-choice scenarios, cost-benefit
  appraisal, funding and delivery options and network optimisation, with every
  cost and benefit reported as a P10/P50/P90 range. Every modelled output is
  synthetic demand, uncalibrated: scenario comparison, not a forecast. Map data
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).
keywords:
  - Saudi Arabia
  - railway
  - transport planning
  - feasibility study
  - cost-benefit analysis
  - reference-class forecasting
  - scenario analysis
  - OpenStreetMap
references:
  - type: software
    title: TrafficTwin Jeddah
    authors:
      - family-names: Alturkestani
        given-names: Tariq
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      Parent project; KSA Rail Twin extends it from one city to the whole Kingdom.
      It is the author's optional private companion project (not public; not
      required to run, test or reproduce KSA Rail Twin).
